  "description": "Your ISO Shimano\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR LEGENDARY ISO, WITH UPDATED FEATURES The ISO (In Search Of) has earned a formidable reputation as the adventure bike that will take you anywhere. It has travelled across continents and endured fearsome terrain. And now it's ready for even more. Sometimes a bike comes along that completely delivers in its capabilities, looks and build quality. The Mason ISO – In Search Of – is one of those bikes. With an Italian hand-built frame, a superb level of finish and detail it nonchalantly comes along and redefines what a drop-bar bike is assumed to be capable of being. off-road.cc | 5/5 The updated ISO2 is a progressive frame and fork with a design allowing use of 29 x 2.6” or 650b x 2.8\" wheels, meaning steeper, rougher and deeper terrain are well within its adventure capabilities. Multiple mounting points, a bespoke load-bearing mudguard, specific rack systems, 160/180 flat-mount braking and 100mm suspension-ready geometry mean that the ISO, once again, is 'progressive' in every sense. Our Shimano ISO builds combine the best of Shimano's mountain bike capability with the comfort of drop-bar braking and shifting.\n\nShimano groupset, combining mountain bike features with drop-bar format\n\nWheelset options include HUNT and DT Swiss, with carbon, aluminium, dynamo and non-dynamo choices\n\nFully ready for performance dynamo lighting. Select 'Mason Luminance Upgrade'\n\nWide range of eyelets in multiple locations, for maximum luggage and fluid carrying capacity. NEW top tube eyelets.",
